u can reverse the subarray $$$[4, 5]$$$. Then $$$a = [2, 3, 2, 3, 1]$$$ and $$$2 \\cdot 1 + 3 \\cdot 3 + 2 \\cdot 2 + 3 \\cdot 4 + 1 \\cdot 2 = 29$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, you don't need to use the reverse operation. $$$13 \\cdot 2 + 37 \\cdot 4 = 174$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example, you can reverse the subarray $$$[3, 5]$$$. Then $$$a = [1, 8, 3, 6, 7, 6]$$$ and $$$1 \\cdot 5 + 8 \\cdot 9 + 3 \\cdot 6 + 6 \\cdot 8 + 7 \\cdot 8 + 6 \\cdot 6 = 235$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1519D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1519/problem/D"}